WEBVTT

00:10:57.257 --> 00:11:00.286
they believe that they are capable
of changing virtual worlds

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:01.976
and not the real world.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.113
That's the problem
that I'm trying to solve.

00:11:04.613 --> 00:11:06.976
There's an economist
named Edward Castronova.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.170
His work is brilliant.

00:11:08.194 --> 00:11:11.096
He looks at why people are investing
so much time and energy

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:12.976
and money in online worlds.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.183
And he says,

00:11:14.207 --> 00:11:17.515
"We're witnessing what amounts to
no less than a mass exodus

00:11:17.539 --> 00:11:19.976
to virtual worlds and online
game environments."

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.189
And he's an economist, so he's rational.

00:11:22.213 --> 00:11:23.650
And he says --

00:11:23.674 --> 00:11:25.317
(Laughter)

00:11:25.341 --> 00:11:27.626
Not like me, I'm a game
designer; I'm exuberant.

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:31.849
But he says that this makes perfect sense,